<p>This is a well written example of the horrific being translated into detached, clinical language, letting the emotional impact come purely from the reader's sensibilities.</p>
<p>As I'm always searching for connections and symbolism as I read, the drug name &quot;Pralilapril&quot; in an article about life-extension called to my mind the name of the Ringworld character Halrloprillalar. Referential, or just wild imagination? It wouldn't be the first Niven reference on the wiki.</p>

